    {
      "sourceRef": "index:3",
      "cellIndex": 3,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "A force $\\vec{F}(t)$ is exerted upon a system with the following characteristics\n\n- m : mass  \n- c : linear dumping coefficient, for a dumping force proportional to velocity  \n- k : spring coefficient",
      "sourceSha256": "8cd04c2ad9a2fe9891acdfb232ac36a3f319e80d55543d23c05dc07cf5a0ab5f",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{F}(t)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:4",
      "cellIndex": 4,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "import sympy as sm # import functions for symbolic manipulations\nfrom sympy.physics import mechanics as me\nme.init_vprinting() # dot notation for velocity and acceleration\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")",
      "sourceSha256": "1e498d2c45c426292100b8937934bc62aeeeb140bfbf97e75fd242de1154367d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "sympy",
          "sympy.physics",
          "warnings"
        ],
        "calls": [
          "me.init_vprinting",
          "warnings.filterwarnings"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:5",
      "cellIndex": 5,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "t = sm.symbols('t') # time\nm, k, c = sm.symbols('m, k, c', positive = True)\nx, F = me.dynamicsymbols('x F')",
      "sourceSha256": "ed169b103d717016b0f26ae1719e32cb8347f1463abc4b1a26e17774ab4b6e5e",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "me.dynamicsymbols",
          "sm.symbols"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:6",
      "cellIndex": 6,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "For a damping proportional to the velocity, the dynamics is described by",
      "sourceSha256": "9637242d73a163fdf27d3dbc23c13fe14f4b4f34dea341ff6e19bb8904f18339",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:7",
      "cellIndex": 7,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_homogeneous = m* x.diff(t,2) + c* x.diff(t) + k* x\nx_EL_forced = sm.Eq(x_EL_homogeneous, F)\nx_EL_forced",
      "sourceSha256": "50e40abe64a7fe9ab87adb56b1b2d5b708c5863b6d30a72404b239d91290544a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "c⋅ẋ + k⋅x + m⋅ẍ = F",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle c \\dot{x} + k x + m \\ddot{x} = F$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq",
          "x.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:8",
      "cellIndex": 8,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "that engineers usually write as",
      "sourceSha256": "8a9f0c88e680909ac8fb2edf056390e3acf6393607ef006608558ad2e1a9c0a3",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:9",
      "cellIndex": 9,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "omega, zeta = sm.symbols('omega zeta', real = True)\nx_EL_ing = sm.Eq(x_EL_forced.lhs/m, x_EL_forced.rhs/m).expand()\nx_EL_ing = x_EL_ing.subs([(k/m, omega**2), (c/m, 2* zeta* omega) ]).simplify()\nx_EL_ing.expand()",
      "sourceSha256": "54d9aa99695673db77f5d75778aac97cd7dc1f20820f7585fbbcf7e329474969",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "F    2                \n─ = ω ⋅x + 2⋅ω⋅ζ⋅ẋ + ẍ\nm                     ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{F}{m} = \\omega^{2} x + 2 \\omega \\zeta \\dot{x} + \\ddot{x}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "expand",
          "simplify",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.symbols",
          "x_EL_ing.expand",
          "x_EL_ing.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:10",
      "cellIndex": 10,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Harmonic forcing\n\nWe saw that when $F=0$ the motion extinguishes more or less rapidly as a function of the damping $c$, but it eventually does so.\nThe solution of the homogeneous equation then produces a **transient solution**.\nIn the presence of $F(t)$ this determines the **steady-state solution** which is what finally dominates the dynamics.\nThe system's response to a harmonic force will be studied first",
      "sourceSha256": "60eb89ae8a16fcdabcf2eeca99e82a1abe97777ff605cdaaae1b0d9266ae5355",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "F=0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "c"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "F(t)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:11",
      "cellIndex": 11,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "> **Reference**\n>- Section 6.5 \"Forced Oscillations\". Jerry B. Marion. Classical Dynamics of particles and systems. Academic Press.",
      "sourceSha256": "30d13ee933baa51473c486c198ae1777d981621fb69b5ba318e373000bf5b2a8",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:12",
      "cellIndex": 12,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "F_0, omega_f = sm.symbols('F_0 omega_f', positive = True)\nF_harmonic = F_0* sm.sin(omega_f* t)\nsm.Eq(F, F_harmonic)",
      "sourceSha256": "0a5cb25a58ceb592a94a69ac50c75facc33ad5b54caf1f8b5c1a16df7f7320e8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "F = F₀⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle F = F_{0} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.sin",
          "sm.symbols"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:13",
      "cellIndex": 13,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The differential equation that we must solve is",
      "sourceSha256": "aeca3e6b24590e8144388987e2b82492fa54dc1453cd96a6ff971278d0e9bbe0",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:14",
      "cellIndex": 14,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_ing_forcedHarmonic = x_EL_ing.expand().subs(F, F_harmonic)\nx_EL_ing_forcedHarmonic",
      "sourceSha256": "d9afdd8a392e98420fc21b3121366295c2272f8e8800c573cd18dc24cf9771a2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "F₀⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)    2                \n───────────── = ω ⋅x + 2⋅ω⋅ζ⋅ẋ + ẍ\n      m                           ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{F_{0} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m} = \\omega^{2} x + 2 \\omega \\zeta \\dot{x} + \\ddot{x}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "subs",
          "x_EL_ing.expand"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:15",
      "cellIndex": 15,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We know that by substituting the particular solution that responds to such forcing $x_p = A_1 \\cos{\\omega_f t} + A_2 \\sin{\\omega_f t}$ into the equation allows us to obtain the $A_i$.\nBut `sympy` can handle the entire process and give us $x = x_h + x_p$ directly.",
      "sourceSha256": "8c298a9f8cf1fe25f6fcf8f14691621c9f19a7cbe5e3cfec6c300d44c9ce17a7",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x_p = A_1 \\cos{\\omega_f t} + A_2 \\sin{\\omega_f t}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "A_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x = x_h + x_p"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:16",
      "cellIndex": 16,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_forcedHarmonic_sol = sm.dsolve(x_EL_ing_forcedHarmonic)\nx_forcedHarmonic_sol",
      "sourceSha256": "c66ca14ff99171e5aa4150ba97b262f403f7a0de722c1add90d7afee0242ea23",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "            ⎛        ________⎞            ⎛       ________⎞                   \n            ⎜       ╱  2     ⎟            ⎜      ╱  2     ⎟                   \n        ω⋅t⋅⎝-ζ + ╲╱  ζ  - 1 ⎠       -ω⋅t⋅⎝ζ + ╲╱  ζ  - 1 ⎠               F₀⋅ω\nx = C₁⋅ℯ                       + C₂⋅ℯ                       + ────────────────\n                                                                ⎛ 4      2    \n                                                              m⋅⎝ω  + 4⋅ω ⋅ω_f\n\n                                                                              \n2                                                                             \n ⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)                       2⋅F₀⋅ω⋅ω_f⋅ζ⋅cos(ω_f⋅t)                    \n──────────────────────── - ──────────────────────────────────────── - ────────\n2  2      2    2      4⎞     ⎛ 4      2    2  2      2    2      4⎞     ⎛ 4   \n ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f  + ω_f ⎠   m⋅⎝ω  + 4⋅ω ⋅ω_f ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f  + ω_f ⎠   m⋅⎝ω  + \n\n                                \n         2                      \n   F₀⋅ω_f ⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)           \n────────────────────────────────\n   2    2  2      2    2      4⎞\n4⋅ω ⋅ω_f ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f  + ω_f ⎠",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = C_{1} e^{\\omega t \\left(- \\zeta + \\sqrt{\\zeta^{2} - 1}\\right)} + C_{2} e^{- \\omega t \\left(\\zeta + \\sqrt{\\zeta^{2} - 1}\\right)} + \\frac{F_{0} \\omega^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)} - \\frac{2 F_{0} \\omega \\omega_{f} \\zeta \\cos{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)} - \\frac{F_{0} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.dsolve"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:17",
      "cellIndex": 17,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The terms that depend on $C_i$ are those of the homogeneous solution which is considered to be present during a **transient** that becomes extinct for $t > 10\\tau$ (10 **relaxation periods**).\nFor later times the solution reaches the **steady state** given by the terms that depend on the forcing.\nWe set $C_1 = C_2 = 0$ to obtain only $x_p(t)$.",
      "sourceSha256": "59fcf0a798094ef80ff53e57d31b47965b812a894243fdab756ebf9e084a25eb",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "t > 10\\tau"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_1 = C_2 = 0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x_p(t)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:18",
      "cellIndex": 18,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_forcedHarmonic = x_forcedHarmonic_sol.subs([('C1', 0), ('C2', 0)])\nx_forcedHarmonic",
      "sourceSha256": "5a64ea46e3464e9517d1e2147695941565ecec8146e75d585874a2b1e6d909e2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                    2                                                         \n                F₀⋅ω ⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)                       2⋅F₀⋅ω⋅ω_f⋅ζ⋅cos(ω_f⋅t)\nx = ──────────────────────────────────────── - ───────────────────────────────\n      ⎛ 4      2    2  2      2    2      4⎞     ⎛ 4      2    2  2      2    \n    m⋅⎝ω  + 4⋅ω ⋅ω_f ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f  + ω_f ⎠   m⋅⎝ω  + 4⋅ω ⋅ω_f ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f\n\n                             2                      \n                       F₀⋅ω_f ⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)           \n───────── - ────────────────────────────────────────\n2      4⎞     ⎛ 4      2    2  2      2    2      4⎞\n  + ω_f ⎠   m⋅⎝ω  + 4⋅ω ⋅ω_f ⋅ζ  - 2⋅ω ⋅ω_f  + ω_f ⎠",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = \\frac{F_{0} \\omega^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)} - \\frac{2 F_{0} \\omega \\omega_{f} \\zeta \\cos{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)} - \\frac{F_{0} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}}{m \\left(\\omega^{4} + 4 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} \\zeta^{2} - 2 \\omega^{2} \\omega_{f}^{2} + \\omega_{f}^{4}\\right)}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "x_forcedHarmonic_sol.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:19",
      "cellIndex": 19,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Response to forcing in the under-damped regime",
      "sourceSha256": "7bc61ef47ab1ab2021fd81f0666fcbc9e4d6704d406a5ba20f5c661e68d37f8f",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:20",
      "cellIndex": 20,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Using the same parameters than in the case without forcing, in the under-damped regime, $\\zeta = 0.2$.",
      "sourceSha256": "61d36e6ca5b22991ab2ba4601229153d3128e88e69dab519ac01fc14855b0235",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\zeta = 0.2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:21",
      "cellIndex": 21,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "k_magnitude = 100 # [N m-1]\nm_magnitude = 1 # [kg]\nzeta_magnitude = 0.2 # [s-1]\n\nparameters ={\n    zeta : zeta_magnitude,\n    omega : sm.sqrt(k_magnitude/m_magnitude),\n    m : m_magnitude\n}\nx_forcedHarmonic_parameters = x_forcedHarmonic.subs(parameters).simplify()\nx_forcedHarmonic_parameters",
      "sourceSha256": "1a54c43d929fdf73225d4f75ccc17ec54dd76d1391935b025c4a28d7ef11bd35",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "       ⎛     2                                                   ⎞\n    F₀⋅⎝- ω_f ⋅sin(ω_f⋅t) - 4.0⋅ω_f⋅cos(ω_f⋅t) + 100.0⋅sin(ω_f⋅t)⎠\nx = ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n                        4            2                            \n                     ω_f  - 184.0⋅ω_f  + 10000.0                  ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = \\frac{F_{0} \\left(- \\omega_{f}^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)} - 4.0 \\omega_{f} \\cos{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)} + 100.0 \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)}\\right)}{\\omega_{f}^{4} - 184.0 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 10000.0}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "simplify",
          "sm.sqrt",
          "x_forcedHarmonic.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {
          "k_magnitude": 100,
          "m_magnitude": 1,
          "zeta_magnitude": 0.2
        },
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:22",
      "cellIndex": 22,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "It becomes of interest how the amplitude of the oscillation of $x$ varies as a function of the forcing parameters.\nEvidently it is linear with the amplitude of the same.\nIt is with its frequency $\\omega_f$ where different behaviors are presented.",
      "sourceSha256": "0216e4dbafbd6e82a3afa38ce778e940bc54a979575de52824bec07a2c851abc",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\omega_f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:23",
      "cellIndex": 23,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "F_0_magnitude = 100 # [N]\nx_forcedHarmonic_omega_f = x_forcedHarmonic_parameters.subs(F_0, F_0_magnitude)",
      "sourceSha256": "0d56dd55f61b044aef67e89f2959048c5e51045962985987fe29c221bb806d05",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "x_forcedHarmonic_parameters.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {
          "F_0_magnitude": 100
        },
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:24",
      "cellIndex": 24,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "To analyze the amplitude it suffices to group the terms with $\\sin{(\\omega_f t)}$ and those with $\\cos{(\\omega_f t)}$ and operate in the same way as when converting complex numbers from rectangular to polar form.\nSince $a^2 \\cos^2{\\omega_f t} + b^2 \\sin^2{\\omega_f t} = a^2 + b^2 = R^2$, where $R$ is the equivalent to the modulus of the complex number.",
      "sourceSha256": "40dad9c2881fe3fe0a27cef2149833a654bc1a4475b3c5bf0786d68d2c96d8fc",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\sin{(\\omega_f t)}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\cos{(\\omega_f t)}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "a^2 \\cos^2{\\omega_f t} + b^2 \\sin^2{\\omega_f t} = a^2 + b^2 = R^2"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "R"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:25",
      "cellIndex": 25,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "rectangular = sm.collect(x_forcedHarmonic_omega_f.rhs.expand(trig=True), [sm.sin(omega_f* t), sm.cos(omega_f* t)], evaluate=False)\nrectangular",
      "sourceSha256": "287226ff3608bf336ece8e4ccbb42c816472ba20e350680bcce18f64c29a5b0e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎧                               2                                             \n⎪                        100⋅ω_f                       10000.0                \n⎨sin(ω_f⋅t): - ─────────────────────────── + ───────────────────────────, cos(\n⎪                 4            2                4            2                \n⎩              ω_f  - 184.0⋅ω_f  + 10000.0   ω_f  - 184.0⋅ω_f  + 10000.0      \n\n                                   ⎫\n                -400.0⋅ω_f         ⎪\nω_f⋅t): ───────────────────────────⎬\n           4            2          ⎪\n        ω_f  - 184.0⋅ω_f  + 10000.0⎭",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left\\{ \\sin{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)} : - \\frac{100 \\omega_{f}^{2}}{\\omega_{f}^{4} - 184.0 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 10000.0} + \\frac{10000.0}{\\omega_{f}^{4} - 184.0 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 10000.0}, \\  \\cos{\\left(\\omega_{f} t \\right)} : - \\frac{400.0 \\omega_{f}}{\\omega_{f}^{4} - 184.0 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 10000.0}\\right\\}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.collect",
          "sm.cos",
          "sm.sin",
          "x_forcedHarmonic_omega_f.rhs.expand"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:26",
      "cellIndex": 26,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "timesSine = rectangular[sm.sin(omega_f* t)]\ntimesCosine = rectangular[sm.cos(omega_f* t)]\nmagnitude = sm.sqrt(timesSine**2 + timesCosine**2).simplify()\nmagnitude",
      "sourceSha256": "fb720680e1447863141de20800f0b4b458c96bf6b4ee61e2c2dfce9433eadf49",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "       _______________________________\n      ╱           4             2     \n1.0⋅╲╱  0.0001⋅ω_f  - 0.0184⋅ω_f  + 1 \n──────────────────────────────────────\n   │          4             2    │    \n   │0.0001⋅ω_f  - 0.0184⋅ω_f  + 1│    ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{1.0 \\sqrt{0.0001 \\omega_{f}^{4} - 0.0184 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 1}}{\\left|{0.0001 \\omega_{f}^{4} - 0.0184 \\omega_{f}^{2} + 1}\\right|}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
